WEBVTT

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.580
That's interesting.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.600
It's more than I expected.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:13.580
Normally, he would have become an invalid long ago, or died.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.370
Of course, we don't want him dying on us now.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.150
The outer edge is complete.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.040
We can't fail here.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.170
How are the insides looking? They're ready, right?

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:29.110
Yes. Even now,
they'd basically be fine,

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:31.370
but we're taking
every precaution.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:36.620
Also, I'll trust you to take
care of that other matter.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.930
We don't know what he'll do.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:40.930
Understood.

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:44.790
Not that I care what happens with it anymore.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.720
But I'll tell them.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:49.820
We can't have an important product destroyed, huh?

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:52.510
You people are greedy.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:53.440
Thank you.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:59.370
It's finally time; I can hardly wait.

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:04.900
Private Tokimune Susumu.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.870
From now on, you are forbidden to pilot Argevollen.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:16.960
Wait a minute!

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.740
Tell me why, please!

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:24.100
If you continue to pilot it,

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:28.350
it will be Argevollen, not the enemy, that kills you.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.170
That's why.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:39.270
Freeze

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:40.770
Why?
Freeze

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:41.370
Freeze

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:43.450
Why can't I pilot Argevollen?
Freeze

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:43.990
Why can't I pilot Argevollen?

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:47.000
What does he mean, it'll kill me?

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:54.580
What if the new enemy model shows up again?

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.630
Do we fight without Arge?

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.380
We may not have a choice.

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:02.390
Why not?

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.510
I'm sorry.

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:10.270
I was so happy with the numbers that I didn't notice.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:12.340
What are you saying?

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.280
I don't understand.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:20.340
Look.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:29.790
Play it.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.240
Damn it!

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:46.180
You tell everyone.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:47.560
Understood.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:52.420
Captain Samonji.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:53.060
What?

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:57.570
Are you really alright with Brigadier General Cayenne's order?

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:07.660
We should just take that thing and...

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:08.890
Suzushiro.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.180
We should just destroy it!

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.630
Understood.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.590
Excuse me.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:26.890
Stop it.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:29.460
Who are you?

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.660
Stop it!

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:34.940
This is me?

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:41.700
Do you remember what happened?

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.330
Back then...

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.420
when I encountered the enemy's new model,

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.100
I heard your voice.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:12.350
Tokimune!

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:13.440
Tokimune,

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.490
what's gotten into you?

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:15.980
Come on, Tokimune!

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:23.400
I don't really remember the rest.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:26.110
What you just heard is what happened after that.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:29.160
You don't even remember how you fought, right?

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:37.500
I remember I was really riled up.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.690
Really excited.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:43.300
It was kind of scary.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:49.180
I can understand why Samonji-san told you not to pilot it.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.670
But how are we supposed to get by without Arge?

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:54.100
Back there...

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:58.230
Back there, you shot Silfy-san.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:03.840
I did?

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:11.200
I shot Silfy-san?

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.290
You just damaged part of her mech.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:14.850
She's unharmed.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.890
Please consider how we're going to handle this in the future.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:33.860
Well, if that's the captain's decision.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:56.040
How is he?

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:58.780
He's still confused.

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:01.920
It's my fault for not telling him anything in advance.

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:03.670
That's not true.

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:09.550
But I was sent here specifically as Argevollen's engineer...

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:14.060
Would you come with me for a bit?

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:21.190
Most soldiers at Pudder supply base 3 are wounded.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:24.850
Unit 8 are essentially the only ones who can fight.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:28.020
As soon as the Seiran and the other vehicles are ready,

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.430
we'll withdraw.

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:30.200
Understood?

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:36.200
Ingelmia's not going to extend their battle lines any further for a single Trail Krieger.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:40.470
I'm told you got a message from Brigadier General Cayenne.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.420
What happened?

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:44.780
It's not easy to explain.

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:47.340
Argevollen?

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:50.720
I'll ask again later.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:52.410
Okay.

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:54.370
Come back safely.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:56.220
Come in.

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.220
I'll contact you again.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:04.230
What is it?

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:08.240
I have a question about the order I was given.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:14.040
During the last battle, I went out of control.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:19.480
Jamie showed me later, and I realized I was acting strange.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:25.250
But I think it was a temporary thing!

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.130
Can you say that for certain?

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:30.630
Can you tell me it will never happen again?

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:41.140
I told you that your sister died during an experiment, right?

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:44.110
Yes, you did.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:47.480
Argevollen was based on the model used in that experiment.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:57.130
How long have you known that?

00:07:58.470 --> 00:07:59.660
From the start.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:05.110
Then why did you let me use it?

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:07.920
I don't understand why you're forbidding me to use it now.

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:11.680
At first, it was a valuable addition to our forces.

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:15.060
But now that there's a possibility that it may go out of control,

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:17.380
I can't let it participate in battle.

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:18.680
That's all.

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:20.950
If you keep piloting it,

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:25.030
it will take you over, like your sister, and you will die.

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:27.690
As your superior officer, I cannot allow that.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:32.320
Just because my sister died doesn't mean I will.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:38.320
I cooperated just like the company told me,

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:41.420
but when I heard Tokimune's voice, I got scared.

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:45.210
It was a voice that echoes in your ears.

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:48.210
It wasn't human. It was like a beast.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:54.400
If Tokimune continues to pilot it, he'll end up like that again, won't he?

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:57.840
That's why the captain forbid him, right?

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.020
I think so.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:05.120
Tokimune...

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:10.860
You knew, didn't you?

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:15.900
That it was based on that other model.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:17.150
What do you mean?

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:21.180
I did.

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:25.120
What are you talking about? You can tell me, can't you?

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.880
Argevollen resulted from the experiment my sister was involved in.

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:35.130
Is that true, Suzushiro-san?

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:40.290
But I wanted to believe it wasn't.

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:44.950
I tricked myself into believing that it was a totally different machine.

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:48.740
That this part was different from Reika-san's.

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:49.970
Or that part.

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:52.860
That was all I could focus on.

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:57.980
But after what happened to you,
all those lies disappeared.

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:00.700
I was just fooling myself.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:04.410
I had to admit that Argevollen was based on that machine.

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:10.420
Tokimune!

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:18.680
She won't forgive me, will she?

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:40.290
What was the captain thinking when he told Tokimune not to pilot Argevollen?

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:41.500
I don't know.

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:43.800
He never says anything.

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:46.460
Is Tokimune's anemia going to be okay?

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:49.080
Maybe Argevollen sucked his blood?

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:50.380
Stop that.

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:53.560
Hey, Geobool fell!

00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:57.460
Geobool's an important fortress on the southwest road!

00:10:58.250 --> 00:10:59.910
Seriously?

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:01.340
This is bad.

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:05.440
Are we just going to...

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:06.880
Stop it.

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:08.620
Hey, help out, too.

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:09.600
Right.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:32.750
Geobool and Dasnia have fallen already.

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:35.240
Shishimoza will fall before long, as well.

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:37.300
We must hurry, as well.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.760
That's right.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:42.740
But we're wasting time here.

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:44.690
On Zarl's orders.

00:11:44.690 --> 00:11:45.620
Yes.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:50.020
Killing one beleaguered platoon won't change anything.

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:53.720
Why is the brigadier general so focused on Argevollen?

00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:54.770
Who knows?

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:58.610
But we'll pay him back someday.

00:11:58.610 --> 00:11:59.410
Yes.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.030
How is the Sturm Alpha?

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:04.250
It needs some repairs,

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:05.500
but it's fine.

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:07.970
Amazing.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:10.040
What are you going to do?

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:13.790
I'm going to carry out our orders.

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:20.770
I'll finish you.

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:28.430
I don't get it.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.680
"Please see appendix B

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:35.400
for information on the physical and mental effects on the pilot."

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:38.440
I looked at appendix B and it didn't make any sense!

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:40.440
Who wrote this manual?

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:47.650
Oh, right! I got that access key!

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:49.950
I can access the data at headquarters.

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:53.960
Here! This is it!

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:59.240
"Human reason unconsciously maintains control over aggressive impulses,

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:04.180
but the functions in the U-Link system that correspond to an AI have no such restrictions.

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:09.180
Thus, the unchecked aggressive impulses are fed back to the pilot,

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:11.220
affecting his mind."

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:15.680
I didn't even understand a single line of that.

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:17.060
What's wrong with you?

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:19.280
Are you an idiot, Jamie Hazaford?

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:21.230
What else?

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:23.140
"These effects can include:

00:13:23.140 --> 00:13:26.790
1: Difficulty in restraining violent impulses.

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:29.250
2: A feeling of confusion..."

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:36.130
I-I'm sorry.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:48.340
Don't interrupt my time with the Sturm.

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:50.800
I-I'm sorry.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:58.310
"3: Disorientation.

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:03.070
4: Destruction of the pilot's personality.

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:07.640
These processes will eventually destroy the pilot's mind.

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:11.610
This process has been given the name of Neural Rideover Syndrome,

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:14.580
or NRS."

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:20.590
NR Syndrome...

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:31.930
Don't interrupt my time with the Sturm.

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:42.460
Is there anything I can help with?

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:44.100
Hey, Tokimune.

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:45.670
You feeling better?

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:47.940
Shouldn't you get some more rest?

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:55.590
What's with him?

00:14:55.590 --> 00:14:58.080
A soldier should move his hands, not his mouth.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:05.650
Okui-san.

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:07.840
Is there anything...

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:12.840
This is my job.

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:14.800
You rest.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:26.980
Good timing.

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:28.780
Silfy-san.

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:33.490
What are you doing?

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:35.730
I'm sorry.

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:39.490
It seems I damaged your machine.

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:41.720
I'd forgotten myself.

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:43.500
I don't know what I was doi—

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:47.780
Help me.

00:15:56.730 --> 00:15:57.760
Senpai!

00:15:58.070 --> 00:16:00.000
Are you okay now?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.010
Yeah.

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:02.670
You're an idiot.

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:05.230
You should've just slept for tonight.

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:08.230
Want me to sleep next to you?

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:12.510
Did you hear that, Kaoru-san?

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:13.740
I did!

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.660
You want to join us?

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:19.340
What do you think?

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:20.750
He's disgusting.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:23.180
Ow!

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:25.000
Stop screwing around.

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:29.530
But now that you're here, we can make use of you!

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:31.820
How long are you going to sit around talking?

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:35.130
We're going to finish this and the other Seiran by morning.

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:37.640
That's crazy.

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:42.250
Why are you just standing there?

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:43.600
Get up here!

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:54.240
We're going to attach that to the body now.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:01.740
Come on, answer! Answer the phone, Suguro-san!

00:17:03.490 --> 00:17:05.460
Okay, connect that!

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:06.590
That's right.

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:08.250
That blue one.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:09.590
Blue one?

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:11.500
It's a miniaturized glass cube tube!

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:12.960
Shut up.

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:15.620
That name's too long to say every single time.

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:17.560
Don't you think this is a waste of time?

00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:19.510
What?

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:24.270
Even if you repair it, Arge won't be going out anymore.

00:17:24.590 --> 00:17:26.330
I heard.

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:29.000
You're forbidden to pilot it, right?

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:29.650
Yes.

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:34.660
Its systems are set up so that only you can pilot it, too.

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:36.190
It's not just a waste of time.

00:17:36.190 --> 00:17:38.160
It's the ultimate waste of time.

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:40.610
I'm sorry.

00:17:40.610 --> 00:17:41.780
But, you know,

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:44.750
wasting time is nothing new.

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:47.790
Our work is just one big waste of time after another.

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.050
Think about it.

00:17:52.390 --> 00:17:54.360
Even after all this maintenance,

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:57.170
a single artillery strike right now

00:17:57.170 --> 00:18:01.800
would blow all the Trail Kriegers up before they had a chance to move.

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:07.820
But we can't neglect even a single screw in a rifle.

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:13.320
That's the one thing we mechanics can do to fight.

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:24.180
You're going to be busy.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:29.210
You'll be a soldier, but you also have to maintain this every day.

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:31.710
Yeah.

00:18:31.990 --> 00:18:34.530
Okay, take the old one down.

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:35.500
Right!

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:41.300
I'm glad.

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:45.180
You're back to normal!

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:46.870
Am I?

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.060
No matter what your orders say,

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:54.070
if everyone doesn't maintain your mech, it won't work.

00:18:55.620 --> 00:18:56.560
Yeah.

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:59.700
You're absolutely, 100% sure that's true?

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:01.970
You're being very pushy.

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:03.410
Of course it's true.

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:08.500
Argevollen has pilot safety functions.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:10.960
NR Syndrome won't happen.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:13.710
But Private Susumu is already...

00:19:13.990 --> 00:19:18.680
You're saying he's physically and psychologically unstable, right?

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:21.000
That's a normal reaction.

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:24.720
It didn't look like a normal reaction to me!

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:27.720
Because you don't know what "abnormal" looks like.

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:33.730
Hazaford-kun?

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:34.980
Yes?

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:38.980
I'd like you and Argevollen to keep working hard.

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:41.470
I'm sure you can do it.

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:44.780
I haven't been able to do anything!

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:02.630
There you are.

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:04.570
Jamie!

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:06.060
Tokimune, come with me.

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:07.260
What?

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:09.270
I need to talk to you.

00:20:14.570 --> 00:20:15.860
What's up?

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:23.200
I did some research after what happened.

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:30.390
Destroy my mind?

00:20:31.260 --> 00:20:34.350
You'll end up like an empty shell.

00:20:34.350 --> 00:20:36.670
But it's set up so that won't happen, right?

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:39.220
That's what Suguro-san said,

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:41.170
but I don't believe it.

00:20:42.210 --> 00:20:44.670
Why?

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:46.430
There's no reason.

00:20:46.710 --> 00:20:48.340
I don't understand.

00:20:48.340 --> 00:20:50.780
You don't have to understand!

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:52.180
What's up with you?

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:53.910
Anyway!

00:20:53.910 --> 00:20:57.600
What if you pilot Arge after I boot it up, and you die?

00:20:57.600 --> 00:21:00.210
What do I do then?

00:21:00.210 --> 00:21:04.070
If you still want to pilot it, you're an idiot! A real idiot!

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:06.450
Stop calling me an idiot!

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:07.870
Well, you're an idiot!

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:09.050
I said don't tell me I'm an idiot!

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:10.070
Well, you're an idiot!

00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:11.370
I said stop saying that!

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:12.450
Idiot! Idiot! Idiot!

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:14.830
Then you're a moron! Moron!

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:30.670
It was a rush job,

00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:35.380
but the Trail Kriegers and vehicles are all repaired and fueled.

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:36.890
Tanita?

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:38.710
The wounded have been treated.

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:41.040
We've got food, weapons, and ammo.

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:42.650
Those who could get a chance to rest did so.

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:44.340
Then...

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:45.780
Get ready to leave.

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:46.780
Yes, sir!

00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:48.660
Captain!

00:21:50.340 --> 00:21:51.280
The enemy's attacking!

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:13.810
We gaze into each other's eyes, and open our hearts.

00:22:13.810 --> 00:22:20.020
A cycle of strength and weakness.

00:22:20.020 --> 00:22:26.650
Your eyes must have adjusted somewhat.

00:22:26.650 --> 00:22:33.330
Verbalize though I may,

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:41.130
I remember that I can't

00:22:41.130 --> 00:22:47.760
rationalize everything

00:22:47.760 --> 00:22:54.930
The world will change, as long as I remain courageous.

00:22:56.180 --> 00:23:02.940
The telepathy I wouldn't have discovered alone,

00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:09.070
leads me ahead, behind your dazzling silouette.

00:23:09.070 --> 00:23:16.450
But even so, I'll keep my unwavering gaze on you;

00:23:16.450 --> 00:23:23.040
It'll reach you someday.

00:23:36.900 --> 00:23:39.850
Defeat
